Let nums be a list of -1, 0, 1, 2, -1, and -4.
Sort nums.
Let n be count of nums.

For every i from 0 to n - 1:
    If i > 0 and item i of nums is item (i - 1) of nums:
        Continue.
    Let lo start at i + 1.
    Let hi be n - 1.
    Repeat while lo < hi:
        Let a be item i of nums.
        Let b be item lo of nums.
        Let c be item hi of nums.
        Let total be a + b + c.
        If total < 0:
            Add 1 to lo.
        Otherwise:
            If total > 0:
                Subtract 1 from hi.
            Otherwise:
                Print a.
                Print b.
                Print c.
                Print "---".
                Repeat while lo < hi and item (lo + 1) of nums is b:
                    Add 1 to lo.
                Repeat while lo < hi and item (hi - 1) of nums is c:
                    Subtract 1 from hi.
                Add 1 to lo.
                Subtract 1 from hi.
